 to watch (often landing on d4, f7). Aim at their pawn.","tips":["Aim for a steady edge by move 12: 65% of games get there, and 44% reach +6 by move 18.","Watch your rook: it is behind 19% of your lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the king's rook (75%), landing on e1, e2, e3.","Aim at their bishop: it is behind 20% of their lost leads, 1.2\u00d7 the usual rate, most often the light-squared bishop (50%). The reply wins it outright 24% of the time. Take it with a pawn.","Material changes hands for you on d4 and f8: build pressure there.","They win material on d4 and f3: keep those squares defended.","Look for the hanging piece: it appears 1.6\u00d7 as often as usual in this opening."],"similar":[],"family":"Blackmar-Diemer Gambit"}